# Dev-watcher ignore list for `pnpm tauri dev`.
#
# The example app depends on the plugin crate by path, so Tauri watches this
# whole repo in addition to `example/matrix-svelte-client/src-tauri`, and it
# reads this file from the common ancestor of the watched folders (the repo
# root). The app also links the plugin's npm package with `workspace:*`, i.e.
# `example/matrix-svelte-client/node_modules/tauri-plugin-matrix-svelte-api` is
# a symlink back here — so the shared `target/` is reachable under a path Tauri
# doesn't recognise as the cargo target dir. Without these patterns every
# artifact cargo writes looks like a source change and dev rebuilds in a loop.
#
# Patterns are matched against the full path (no parent-directory matching),
# hence the `**/` prefixes and `/**` suffixes.
**/node_modules/**
**/target/**
**/.git/**
**/.svelte-kit/**
example/matrix-svelte-client/build/**
